"""
Tutorial 2 — Linearization.

Linearizes the open-loop F16 plant about trim, from the four control inputs with
aerodynamic effect (uT, uEl, uAil, uRud; the leading-edge flap is inert in this plant) to
the 12 measured outputs (yn..yR). It reuses the design model `LQGDemo` (step 3) with the
loop opened at the 12 measurement analysis points: the plant keeps its trim command
inputs and the controller feedback is cut, so the result is the bare plant P, not the
closed loop.

Output: poles, zeros, and Bode/step responses of the linearized plant.
"""
analysis TutorialLinearize
  extends DyadControlSystems.LinearAnalysis(inputs = ["uT", "uEl", "uAil", "uRud"], outputs = ["yn", "ye", "yalt", "yphi", "ypitch", "ypsi", "yvt", "yalpha", "ybeta", "yP", "yQ", "yR"], loop_openings = ["yn", "ye", "yalt", "yphi", "ypitch", "ypsi", "yvt", "yalpha", "ybeta", "yP", "yQ", "yR"])
  model = LQGDemo()
relations
end
